{"chunk_id": "507117d8f354", "text": "Hidden in the flowering Ashoka grove of Lanka, Hanuman waits in a tree, reasoning that Sita\u2014devoted to nature and grief-stricken in captivity\u2014must eventually come to the nearby pool. From his perch he surveys Ravana\u2019s magnificent garden, described like a second heaven, filled with blooming trees, birds, temples, and shining pools. Amid this splendor he suddenly sees a sorrowful woman in soiled yellow silk, surrounded by fearsome female demons. Emaciated from fasting and grief yet still radiant, she appears like a flame veiled in smoke. Hanuman studies her carefully, comparing her features with what he knows of Rama\u2019s beloved, and concludes that this suffering figure must indeed be Sita. The moment is pivotal: after the long search, the divine mission of locating her finally succeeds.\nHidden in the Ashoka grove, Hanuman finally spots the sorrowful, captive Sita surrounded by demonesses and confirms her identity.\nThemes: discovery of Sita, grief and captivity, devotion to Rama, hope in despair, Hanuman's vigilance", "vector": [0.004307278897613287, -0.021380068734288216, -0.002709095599129796, 0.0015233465237542987, -0.004250735510140657, 0.015206856653094292, -0.01974363625049591, 0.0005392414168454707, -0.0159918125718832, -0.010916207917034626, 0.00014956985251046717, 0.014727900736033916, 0.0033576819114387035, 0.013118076138198376, -0.009293079376220703, 0.0037917359732091427, 0.049545351415872574, -0.005444800015538931, 0.03177075460553169, -0.027140846475958824, -0.012479468248784542, 0.006672124844044447, -0.011827555485069752, -0.007882819510996342, -0.018453115597367287, -0.00817551463842392, 0.030094409361481667, -0.042653702199459076, 0.02420058846473694, -0.016178073361516, -0.015765639021992683, -0.023255981504917145, -0.030307279899716377, -0.01813381165266037, -0.017016246914863586, 0.008015862666070461, -0.0010626838775351644, -0.010942816734313965, 0.004962517414242029, -0.014807727187871933